25NOV2024 @hanoihantrakul
Implementation notes:

When I first tried to spike this system, I only worked with 
mono signals and magnitude spectrum only. I never got round
to doing experiments with complex representations.

I used data 2255 which was the same data used to train the tokenizer. 
This was for the 24khz mono configuration.

I used data 5495 which is the same data used for diffusion training. 
This is the 44.1khz mono configuration.

Note that I had to comment out some code in the dataloader to make this work
but I did not commit it to master because this was more of a spike. 
In `recipes/datasets/mcc/mix_mkii.py` line 271 I had to comment out
the `get_text()` function.

def __call__(self, item: Dict[str, Any]) -> Generator:
        try:
            text = self.get_text(item)
        except Exception as e:
            self._update_stats(skipped=True, message=f"Error loading text: {e}")
            return
        try:
            ...

These configs reconstruct audio using the `torch_wav2spec()` function, which is not compatible
with GriffinLim inversion.